      "math_academy_id": "q-103814",
      "knowledge_point_id": "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326",
      "knowledge_point": "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$ Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\n- $y=1$ is the minimum value of the function. $$\n- $x=9\\pi $ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n- The function takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13940224/assets/066fe6ce8a65927436d64753ec4e61bfea257405e4b2f81554ac8341572bcf15.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty )$, therefore the function doesn't have a minimum value. Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi $ for any integer $n$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence statement II is true.\n\n- The cosecant takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$ Hence statement III is true.",
